# Docker, shell and env files must keep LF endings.
#
# Reason: with Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true), a CRLF checkout of
# Dockerfile.dev/Dockerfile.test injects a stray carriage return into every line
# of the shell entrypoints those images generate with printf, which breaks
# container start-up. A CRLF .env is worse: docker compose reads the trailing \r
# as part of DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY, and that key can never be "fixed" later without
# losing access to the encrypted database.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly force LF for the files that matter to containers.
[Dd]ockerfile*      text eol=lf
*.dockerignore     text eol=lf
.dockerignore      text eol=lf
.env.example       text eol=lf
.env.test          text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
*.sh               text eol=lf
*.service          text eol=lf
nginx.conf         text eol=lf
Caddyfile          text eol=lf

# Never touch binary payloads.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wasm binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
